        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(ui): Codex-style minimal sidebar — pinned/chats groups, icon footer, no brand header",
        "body": "Related: #100287\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe customizable sidebar from #100296 still carried chrome that competed with the conversation: a duplicate brand header, a boxed Recent section, three default-pinned destinations, and a vertically labeled utility footer. Pinned chats also shared the same nine-row budget as ordinary recents, so common pin counts displaced recent chats and larger pin sets could disappear entirely.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis makes the sidebar session-first. It starts with New session, separates Pinned from Chats, keeps every pin plus nine ordinary recent chats, and leaves only Overview pinned by default. More and the customize menu keep every destination reachable. Settings, Docs, pairing, and connection status move into one compact footer row; the redundant Recent-collapse preference and brand header are removed.\n\nThe branch was rebuilt on current `main` without the already-landed #100296 commits, reducing the review surface to this follow-up.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThe default sidebar now presents New session, pinned chats, recent chats, All sessions, Overview, More, and a one-line utility footer. Custom route pins still persist and reset correctly; desktop rail mode and the tablet drawer remain operable. The production change removes 161 more lines than it adds outside tests and generated localization output.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox-through-Crabbox `tbx_01kwt2b7b011z2cfe4w0fbxpha`: focused session-navigation unit coverage, both mocked-Gateway sidebar E2Es, UI typecheck, and the 20-locale consistency check passed.\n- The same exact rebuilt branch passed `pnpm check:changed` (core production/tests/docs lanes, including typecheck and full core lint fanout) in 7m58s.\n- Source-blind browser validation passed desktop default/More/customization, reload persistence, reset, collapsed rail, and settled 900 px tablet drawer behavior; six screenshots captured locally.\n- Fresh Codex autoreview (`gpt-5.5`) of the complete branch reported no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Regression coverage proves all pinned sessions remain visible while nine unpinned recent chats retain their independent budget.\n",
